## 2026-08-19

### 1055 — Relay supply-chain audit closes reviewer fail-open paths (TASK-260715-vtot05)
- REVIEW REWORK: Every fixed relay/build/compiler/standard-library component now matches an authoritative pinned Git or toolchain record across identity, revision/version, content hash, exact HTTPS source allowlist, SPDX license, checked-in license hash, notice obligation, and distribution class. Lockstep edits to generated inventory/provenance can no longer legitimize a mismatched source record.
- RUNTIME GATE: Rework 03 keeps complete classification of exact `App/`, `Sources/`, and `relay/` roots and replaces call-shaped raw-text matching with comment-free per-language lexical tokens. C-family scanning normalizes escaped newlines and rejects direct references, address-taking, macro aliases, and recursively fragmentable token pasting for libcurl and process APIs; Swift rejects `Process` type references and ambiguous `Data`/`String` `contentsOf` constructor references; Objective-C rejects dynamic selector/reflection paths; and Go forbidden imports remain alias/group/raw-string independent. Unknown/new kinds, symlinks, and non-regular entries fail while explicit local `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` reads remain allowed.
- CLAIM BOUNDARY: The gate verifies the complete classified repository runtime surface against its enumerated forbidden mechanisms. It is not a general semantic proof for arbitrary future languages; any unclassified file must fail until policy and scanner review.
- VERIFICATION: Nineteen focused Python tests include compiler/typechecker/preprocessor-backed regressions for C macro aliases, escaped identifiers, function pointers, token-pasted libcurl, Swift process/type initializer aliases, and Objective-C split dynamic selectors, plus both prior reviewer rounds and adjacent scope/classification controls. Supply-chain/asset audits, 26 asset-manifest Python tests, 4 Swift manifest tests, all relay Go packages, 35 relay-release tests, Go vet, unsigned Swift build, Black, Swift format, Actionlint, JSON parsing, privacy scan, diff check, and byte-identical double generation are the handoff gates.
- BOARD ANOMALY: `task-board validate` exits 0 while reporting the pre-existing `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` stored `to-dev` versus child aggregate `development` mismatch. The task contract forbids weakening validation or falsifying parent dependencies, so the anomaly remains separate from this ready-for-review handoff.

### 1035 — Relay assets bind exact source/build provenance to deferred M5 release controls (TASK-260715-vtot05)
- SUPPLY CHAIN: The accepted four-asset archive now shares one deterministic linkage digest with the pinned relay source/tree/file hashes, historical build-recipe revision and files, Go 1.26.5 compiler/internal-linker archive, standard-library-only lock, target matrix, build command, scoped dependency inventory, and generated product notice input. The builder is explicitly repository-local Darwin arm64 with no container/base image; build execution remains offline.
- POLICY: M2 owns source pinning, reproducibility, asset hashes, and notices. Signing (`TASK-260715-3sk5cd`), notarization (`TASK-260715-387eof`), release attestation (`TASK-260715-1gzhnk`), and distribution approval (`TASK-260715-312u2k`) remain concrete M5 scopes; this task performs none of them.
- GATE: `make relay-supply-chain-audit` fails on lock/source/recipe/toolchain/license/notice/inventory/provenance/manifest drift, sensitive or workstation data, mutable dependency URLs, and application runtime code-download surfaces. Deterministic generation is byte-idempotent, the focused Python/Swift asset suites pass, and the pinned relay Go tests plus vet remain green.
- BOARD ANOMALY: Task/story development status cannot aggregate to epic `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` because its unfinished epic dependencies prohibit the required development transition; the explicit repair attempt exited 1 and the board leaves the blocked-by-dependency epic at backlog. This does not change the task evidence or justify weakening a supply-chain gate.

### 0616 — Generated-project workflow is reproducible and preserves signing/migration boundaries (TASK-260715-d6x51z)
- DOCUMENTATION: `docs/generated-workspace-foundation.md` is now the developer authority for clean checkout, pinned tools, generation, unsigned builds/tests, harness and relay smoke, four relay cross-builds, target ownership, non-secret Gate P0 inputs, dependency updates, artifact locations, troubleshooting, current validation limits, and legacy coexistence. `README.md` links the full gate and `CONTRIBUTING.md` now distinguishes the macOS 15/Swift tools 6.1 v2 baseline from legacy macOS 14/Swift 5.10.
- VERIFICATION: On revision `d18847cd6d7f3b84bdd807eddbca37d9259945de`, the exact `make credential-free-validate LEGACY_ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy` gate exits 0 after checksum-pinned relay bootstrap. Relay packaging, deterministic generation, unsigned Debug/Release macOS targets, generated target contracts, all shared Swift tests, Release build, native packaging, detached legacy v0.1.0 preservation/guard/tests/Release build, focused harness suite, inline redacted harness smoke, diff checks, and board validation pass.
- FAIL-CLOSED FINDINGS: Before relay bootstrap, workspace/macOS/command-contract gates correctly exited 2/2/1 for the missing verified relay input. The first drafted harness example exited 64 because its profile reference was not an opaque UUID and was corrected to a synthetic UUID. Direct validation of the developer's independently evolving sibling legacy checkout exited 2, while the gate-owned detached v0.1.0 clone passed; clean-checkout docs now clone the tag explicitly.
- SAFETY: Production signing, physical Gate P0, Developer ID archive, notarization, DMG publication, iOS, installation, app/provider launch, VPN preference save/activation, route mutation, and DNS mutation were not run. Documentation makes no shipping claim and routes physical work only through dedicated-host gate `TASK-260819-25e1ys`.

### 0505 — Accepted provider graph passes the clean architecture matrix; harness cancellation test is flaky (TASK-260715-nphtib)
- VERIFICATION: A fresh local `--no-hardlinks` clone of authoritative revision `7dc73ac6e7325f86a4a178a0558619f0fc9d1490` passed `make credential-free-validate` in 310.40 seconds. Evidence covers the exact six macOS-only workspace schemes, four generated targets, Debug/Release configurations, unsigned host/provider builds, deterministic double generation, static universal provider linkage, verified relay resources, 443 Swift tests, and detached legacy `v0.1.0` test/build. Product Swift coverage is 89.97% lines, 89.62% functions, and 82.11% regions; strict product Swift formatting and board validation pass.
